# Line endings are fixed in the repository, whatever the checkout's platform: the build scripts,
# the guest's /etc files and the patches break with CRLF (bash reads `\r` as part of a command,
# `git apply` stops matching). Only Windows batch files keep CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.otf binary
*.wasm binary
*.cpio binary

# The executable bit is not something .gitattributes can carry. A checkout that lost it still
# builds, because build.py runs every script through bash and restores the bit on start;
# `python3 build.py perms --git` records it in the index for the next commit.
